Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 08:01:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/14] =?UTF-8?q?perf:=20tune=20parallel=20sync=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=2016=20clients,=20speculative=20prefetch=20alignment,?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20RAII=20safety?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- PARALLEL_FETCH_COUNT 8 → 16 (more HTTP clients = less head-of-line blocking)
- pull_blocks: req.max_block_count = 1000 (≈17 MB resp, below 50 MB server cap
  and epee object limits; matches PREFETCH_BATCH)
- pull_and_parse_next_blocks: speculative prefetch now runs CONCURRENTLY with
  main pull_blocks (previously serial), saving 5–15 s per iter.
  Speculative batches start at prev_blocks_start_height + prev_blocks.size()
  + PREFETCH_BATCH - 1; gap-validator drops misaligned batches cleanly.
- RAII scope guards on all spec/prefetch/fast_refresh thread vectors so an
  exception between launch and join can no longer trigger std::terminate
  (fixes crash observed when Ledger disconnected mid-sync).
- epee http_abstract_invoke: per-request X-Perf-Req-Id + send/recv epoch_ms
  headers for cross-machine correlation; MCWARNING("global", ...) to bypass
  net.http category filtering; object/field/string limits 65536*3 → 65536*16
  (needed for 1000-block pruned responses with many ring/output structs).
